#edb/ref 17592186105686 :question/id #uuid "1da70111-4e82-5fe4-b4be-08d0cc6f1110" :question/math-academy-id "e-8330"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dbeb43f0-d94d-5ee0-b7fb-fbbe0a804cb7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048842}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106539} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106541} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503709} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514410} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514471} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514478}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"} :step/id #uuid "2a2959f5-bf52-5984-b73d-213061968d0f" :step/math-academy-id 31130 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106809}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106807 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105848 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105687 :question/id #uuid "192e6748-24e3-5688-87d9-cdf379e24101" :question/math-academy-id "e-8332"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0016464f-27c3-5f1b-a6d3-fe7b5ffb7fbd" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051084}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106537} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106543} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514396} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514398} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514429} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514477}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"} :step/id #uuid "c2857b6c-e2ae-51ac-8fed-6318597083dc" :step/math-academy-id 31133 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106805}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106808 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107119 :tutorial/content "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nSince the hyperbolic functions are defined in terms of exponential functions, we can easily calculate their derivatives. \n\nThe derivatives of the basic hyperbolic functions are as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x) & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) & ={sech}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use these results to find the derivative of the following function:\n\n$$\ny = \\sinh{x} - 2\\cosh{x}\n$$\n\nUsing the usual properties of derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "df316238-1ead-50db-80ec-d47656e6acad" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5207 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "5afd4693-e1ad-5f9f-94cf-364eceabce7d" :step/math-academy-id 32691 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106804}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106809 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107120 :tutorial/content "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n%$\n\nWe would like the prove the following result:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\sinh{x}) = \\cosh x\n$$\n\nTo do this, we revert to the definition of the hyperbolic sine:\n\n$$\n\\sinh x = \\dfrac{1}{2}(e^x-e^{-x}).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proof for the derivative of the hyperbolic cosine is very similar. You may wish to try it for yourself." :tutorial/id #uuid "11e38932-d6a4-5649-bbbe-205fb1bad98d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5221 :tutorial/title "Deriving the Formula for the Derivative of the Hyperbolic Sine"} :step/id #uuid "e126b8c5-2d87-5d89-bbf3-8265d50ec279" :step/math-academy-id 32711 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106810}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106810 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107121 :tutorial/content "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nWe would like the prove the following result:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\tanh{x}) = \\sech^2{x}\n$$\n\nWe do this using the definition of the hyperbolic tangent. The most convenient definition to work with for this purpose is\n\n$$\n\\tanh{x} = \\dfrac{e^{2x}-1}{e^{2x}+1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equation with respect to $x$ using the quotient rule, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({e}^{2x}-1)^{′}\\cdot ({e}^{2x}+1)-({e}^{2x}-1)\\cdot ({e}^{2x}+1)^{′}}{({e}^{2x}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2{e}^{2x})({e}^{2x}+1)-({e}^{2x}-1)(2{e}^{2x})}{({e}^{2x}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{2x}-2{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{2x}}{({e}^{2x}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{2x}}{({e}^{2x}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}+1})}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}})}^{2} \\\\  & ={sech}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "2a7389d5-4ba5-5fd7-8edb-b983483e6099" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5223 :tutorial/title "Deriving the Formula for the Derivative of the Hyperbolic Tangent"} :step/id #uuid "0acbbc47-60c9-5d52-bac4-6df37c07940b" :step/math-academy-id 32713}] :activity/title "Differentiating Hyperbolic Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105995}]}
